id: how_we_did_this_work
title: How we did this work
----

----
id: balancing_groups
----
### Balancing each group, fairly

Our *Impact of AI on work* engagement had two phases. In Phase 1, any Californian could share their views through an open online survey. In Phase 2, smaller groups of those who responded would be invited to live discussions.

We needed to decide who to invite. And we needed to choose fairly, while creating balanced groups.

So we used an approach called sortition, which is like how courts choose juries. It is built on two equally important ideas:

- **Representation:** We set demographic goals based on California population estimates. This would make the final list of invitees reflect the diversity of the state. Criteria included things like age, geography, and field of work.
- **Randomness:** Within those goals, everyone who fit had an equal chance of being selected.

These principles ensured we wouldn’t hear only from those who responded first. It let us build a fairly-chosen list that roughly reflected Californians as a whole.
